+## Session backlog
+
+A sticky session collects asks one turn at a time, and an ask that lives only in the chat gets dropped. The chat that runs n-mode, never a delegate, keeps a backlog file of the user's mid-session messages per `references/session-backlog.md`. The run's opening request goes through Interview instead. Read that file when the first message after the opening request arrives. Each such message that asks for a change or gives feedback becomes a draft row before any other step, and a task only after the user confirms your restatement of it. On each new turn while a row is open, read the backlog and the row's intent, when it has one, before anything else. End a reply with the title lines of the rows that changed state that turn. Session pickup reads `<root>/.claude/worktrees/backlog.md`, when it exists, as open work at its step 2, along with that reference, and the resume note of Pause safely points at it.
